<p>Kathleen Creel, recently assistant professor of philosophy and computer science at <a href="https://cssh.northeastern.edu/philosophy/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Northeastern University</a>, has moved to the <a href="https://lsa.umich.edu/philosophy" target="_blank" rel="noopener">University of Michigan</a>, where she is now associate professor of philosophy.<span id="more-58182"></span></p>
<p><img decoding="async" class="wp-image-58184 aligncenter" src="https://dailynous.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/creel-kathleen-photo-1024x1014.jpg" alt="" width="500" height="495" srcset="https://dailynous.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/creel-kathleen-photo-1024x1014.jpg 1024w, https://dailynous.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/creel-kathleen-photo-300x297.jpg 300w, https://dailynous.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/creel-kathleen-photo-150x150.jpg 150w, https://dailynous.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/creel-kathleen-photo-768x760.jpg 768w, https://dailynous.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/creel-kathleen-photo-1536x1521.jpg 1536w, https://dailynous.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/creel-kathleen-photo-400x396.jpg 400w, https://dailynous.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/creel-kathleen-photo.jpg 2000w" sizes="(max-width: 500px) 100vw, 500px" /></p>
<p>Professor Creel&#8217;s work focuses on the moral, political, and epistemic implications of machine learning, and on other topics in philosophy of science and the history of early modern philosophy. You can learn more about her work <a href="https://kathleenacreel.com/research.html" target="_blank" rel="noopener">here</a> and <a href="https://philpeople.org/profiles/kathleen-a-creel" target="_blank" rel="noopener">here</a>.</p>
<p>She took up her new position at Michigan on August 25th.</p><p>The post <a href="https://dailynous.com/2026/08/26/creel-from-northeastern-to-michigan/">Creel from Northeastern to Michigan</a> first appeared on <a href="https://dailynous.com">Daily Nous</a>.</p>